When the theme was first annouced, I drew a blank for a game idea for a week or two.

Hello! Long term lurker here (as you can see from my no posts
), but I'd just like to clarify that if I use ChatGPT to help me work on my plugins (ex. getting data from notetags, figuring out a "length is undefined" error, etc.) would I be disqualified? I've used it for my workflow for sometime, but it just hit me that it was still AI, or is it exclusively for art related GenAI (no issues here, been using hiddenone's and Avy's stuff which are fantastic!).
Sorry if this is a bit of a sensitive topic (as I've seen), but just wanted to confirm this before I continued working on more of my plugins for my entry. Thanks!

@Requiscence
, you would most definitely be DQ'ed if you did that. It literally says "no AI assets" in the rules, and AI plug-in files are technically assets, albeit as game code. So if you even try, you're gonna be ****ed over before you even have a chance. The rule is strict for a reason.
TL/DR: If AI is used for ANY portion of the game, no matter how much, you're not going to be eligible to enter it.
